      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg TID. The 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day, a common max in practice)\n- **500 mg PO BID or TID**, if you're starting or titrating\n\nIf 1,700 mg TID is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
